Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:16:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: panorama cover shapes notify per version, not per
 map read
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every learnt ratio was written into a snapshot map. Measure read that
map for every row, and tracking walked every id during composition, so
one cover decode recomposed the shelf and remeasured every lane.

Learnt and committed ratios are plain maps under a lock. Measure
subscribes only to PanoramaMasonryContentEpoch, which increments when a
committed cover crosses the wide/tall band. A same-band update changes
the committed value and the cell's own float state, and does not bump
the epoch. The threshold stays RatioSwitchToPanorama.

与 mihon-harmony 0026 同源. Mihon names that threshold
RATIO_SWITCH_TO_PANORAMA in CommonMangaItem; Anikku already defines it
as RatioSwitchToPanorama in MangaCover.
